- ArrayBuffer adoption from external bytes has a fallible factory that consumes the destructor on both success and allocation failure.
- ArrayBuffer byte leases keep backing storage alive and address-stable, reject direct detachment, and defer shrinking-tail decommit until release. Transfer defaults to rejection; explicitly copy-permitting leases preserve source attachment and copy resizability and maximum length. Any overlapping strict lease still rejects transfer.
- ArrayBuffer transfer to a fixed-length wrapper prepares allocation and wrapper registration before detaching the source; fallible unshared buffer factories also handle native wrapper allocation failure.
- GlobalObjectMethodTable carries Bun's transpiled-module analysis hook instead of a weak embedder symbol.
- The ordinary microtask queue accepts native tasks and invokes GlobalObjectMethodTable hooks to execute or release their owned contexts, including termination and realm teardown.
- StringImpl exposes layout accessors from which Bun exports the refcount, length, data, and flags constants.
- ExternalStringImpl static factories mark the wrapper immortal as well as preserving its external buffer.
- RunLoopBun consumes the generated strong timer export declarations.
- RegExp exposes a read-only classification of construction-time memory exhaustion so URLPattern preserves OOM instead of reporting invalid syntax.
- ErrorInstance's embedder stack formatter commits materialization only after success and preserves captured frames when formatting throws or terminates.
- Timezone overrides expose an allocation-free commit for identifiers validated by Bun's fallible preparation.
- Class-name inspection exposes an exception-preserving entry point for stack formatting.

